Lab: Predicting Flight Arrival Delays
Objective
 
In this lab, we will build a regression model to predict the arrival delay (ArrDelay) of a flight. You will perform data cleaning, feature engineering, and evaluate your model’s performance.
 
Dataset: AI-Fundamentals-Updated/data/flights.zip at main · monika-4dec/AI-Fundamentals-Updated
 
Prerequisites
Python 3.x
Libraries: pandas, scikit-learn, matplotlib, seaborn
 
Step 1: Data Exploration & Preprocessing
Before building a model, you need to understand the relationship between the variables.
Handle Missing Values: Check if there are any null values in ArrDelay or DepDelay.
Correlation Analysis: Visualize the relationship between departure delay and arrival delay.
Tip: In aviation, DepDelay is usually the strongest predictor of ArrDelay.
Data Cleaning: Remove columns that are redundant or "leaky" (information that wouldn't be known before a flight lands), such as ArrDel15 or Cancelled.
 
Step 2: Feature Selection
Choose your Features (X) and your Target (y).
Target ($y$): ArrDelay
Features ($X$): DepDelay, CRSDepTime, CRSArrTime, Month, DayOfWeek.
 
Exercise: Convert categorical data like Carrier or OriginState into numerical values using One-Hot Encoding if you wish to include them in the model.
 
Step 3: Train/Test Split
Split your data to ensure your model generalizes well to unseen flights.
